WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.240
For more than 50 years, Bond girls have given
Agent 007 a run for his money in the race

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.500
to see who can be more compelling on the big
screen.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:11.580
In celebration of that incredible legacy,
and the many actresses who've contributed

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.480
to it, let's see what those Bond girls are
up to today..

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.180
Ursula Andress helped set the template for Bond girls when she appeared as Honey Ryder

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.500
in 1962's Dr. No.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.740
The scene in which she walks out of the ocean
in a bikini is one of the franchise's most

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.020
memorable entrances.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:31.900
She continued acting regularly through the
1980s, most prominently in 1981's Clash of

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:32.640
the Titans.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.500
Her acting work slowed in the '90s, and she
hasn't made a film since 2005.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.780
An Italian model and beauty queen, Dianela
Bianchi's biggest acting role came as Tatiana

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.880
Romanova in the second Bond film, From Russia
With Love.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:51.230
She retired from acting in 1970 to marry Italian
businessman Alberto Cameli, though she has

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.620
since appeared in documentary footage discussing
her time as a Bond girl.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.980
For many, Honor Blackman as Pussy Galore,
a villain who proves Bond's equal and ultimately

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:03.520
switches sides for him in Goldfinger, is the
quintessential Bond girl.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.240
Since that unforgettable role, Blackman has
continued working regularly on stage and screen,

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.040
and she's also enjoyed a singing career.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:14.480
Her most recent acting appearance was in an
episode of You, Me &amp; Them in 2015.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.700
As Jill Masterson in Goldfinger, Shirley Eaton
didn't have much screen time, but her death

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.960
while covered in gold paint made her an icon.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.300
After Bond, Eaton continued acting in films
like The Blood of Fu Manchu before retiring

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.140
in 1969 to focus on raising her two sons.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:33.480
She published an autobiography in 1999, and
she also enjoys painting and sculpture.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.999
Thunderball had a memorable and sexy villain
in the form of Luciana Paluzzi as SPECTRE

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.580
agent Fiona Volpe.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.920
The resulting fame kept her acting throughout
the '60s and '70s.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.880
Since 1980, she's been married to American
businessman Michael Jay Solomon.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.689
She doesn't have any onscreen acting credits
since then, though she has given interviews

00:01:51.689 --> 00:01:53.520
reflecting on her time as a Bond girl.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.860
Diana Rigg was already a star by the time
she appeared as Bond's bride Tracy in 1969's

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.480
On Her Majesty's Secret Service.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.800
Since then, she's continued to work steadily
in film, TV, and theater.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:10.170
She became a dame in 1994, and her most famous
recent role was her Emmy-nominated turn as

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.600
Queen Olenna Tyrell on Game of Thrones.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:18.120
Jill St. John played diamond smuggler Tiffany
Case in Diamonds Are Forever, making her the

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.980
first American Bond girl.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.480
She continued acting steadily until 2002,
at which point she largely retired.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.280
Since 1990 she's been married to actor Robert
Wagner.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:32.659
Her most recent screen appearance was as Mrs.
Claus alongside Wagner as Santa in the 2014

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.260
Hallmark movie Northpole.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:40.100
Jane Seymour rocketed to worldwide fame in
1973 as the enigmatic Solitaire

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.560
in Roger Moore's James Bond debut, Live and
Let Die.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:48.760
Since then she's worked regularly in both
film and TV, most famously as the title character

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.520
on Dr. Quinn, Medicine Woman.

00:02:50.969 --> 00:02:55.040
She's also an author of self-help and children's
books, and she designed the "Open Hearts Collection"

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.400
of jewelry for Kay Jewelers.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.800
Britt Ekland's role as Miss Goodnight in The
Man with the Golden Gun cemented her status

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.680
as a sex symbol, and she continued acting
well into the '80s.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:09.340
She was also famous for her high-profile relationships
with Peter Sellers and Rod Stewart.

00:03:09.359 --> 00:03:13.659
In the past decade, she's shown up on a few
reality TV shows, including the Swedish series

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:15.099
Let's Dance in 2018.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:22.160
Barbara Bach achieved fame as Agent Anya Amasova
in 1977's The Spy Who Loved Me.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:26.520
She continued to act in the '80s, but she
hasn't appeared in a film since To the North

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.620
of Katmandu in 1986.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.160
Since 1981, she's been married to former Beatle
Ringo Starr.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:37.340
She's also been active in charity work, forming
the Self Help Addiction Recovery Program in

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:37.860
1991.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:43.139
Lois Chiles was offered the female lead in
The Spy Who Loved Me, but she was taking a

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.820
hiatus from acting at the time and turned
it down.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:51.980
But then a couple of years later, she accepted
the role of Dr. Holly Goodhead in 1979's Moonraker.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:56.800
She continued acting throughout the '80s and
'90s, and her most recent film role was in

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.140
2006's Kettle of Fish.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:04.460
French actress Carole Bouquet achieved international
fame as the vengeance-seeking Melina Havelock

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:06.980
in 1981's For Your Eyes Only.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:11.360
She's continued acting in dozens of films,
plays, and TV series ever since.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:16.680
In 2014 she served on the jury of the Cannes
Film Festival, and in 2017, she played a serial

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.100
killer in the French miniseries La Mante.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:24.620
Maud Adams is unique among the actresses on
this list for playing two different Bond girls.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.160
First she was Andrea Anders in The Man with
the Golden Gun, and then she was the title

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.660
crime lord in 1983's Octopussy.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:35.460
She also even had an uncredited cameo in A
View to a Kill.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.400
She continued to act regularly until largely
retiring in the late 2000s.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:45.080
Tanya Roberts appeared as Stacey Sutton in
1985's A View to a Kill, and she continued

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.530
to act regularly throughout the '90s before
landing her most famous recent role as Donna's

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.320
mother Midge on That '70s Show.

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:55.560
She ultimately left the show in 2001, though
she did return for a brief run of episodes

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.620
in 2004.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.280
Her acting career has been largely inactive
since then.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.940
In A View to a Kill, Grace Jones was instantly
memorable as the deadly May Day.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.860
She's continued to appear sporadically in
films and TV in the subsequent decades.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:12.280
But her major pursuit, as it was before Bond,
is music.

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:17.979
Since 1977, she's released 10 studio albums
and remains one of the most distinctive performers

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:18.980
of her generation.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:26.120
In 1987, Maryam d'Abo kicked off the Timothy
Dalton era as Kara Milovy in The Living Daylights.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.500
She's continued to work as an actress and
model ever since.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.780
In 2002, she hosted the documentary Bond Girls
Are Forever.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:38.120
In 2007, she suffered a near-fatal brain hemorrhage,
from which she thankfully later recovered.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.900
Carey Lowell played Pam Bouvier in 1989's
License To Kill, and she's continued to act

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:44.500
to this day.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:49.300
She had a major role as Jamie Ross on Law
&amp; Order beginning in 1996.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:53.360
In the mid-2010s, her divorce from Richard
Gere was the subject of a three-year legal

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:53.860
battle.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:58.020
As of 2018 she's returned to TV with roles
on Blue Bloods and Bull.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:03.960
In 1995 the Pierce Brosnan era of Bond began,
complete with a new Moneypenny in the form

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.440
of Samantha Bond, who appeared in all four
Brosnan films.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.360
Since the Brosnan era ended, she's continued
to act in a little bit of everything.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:15.860
Her most recent high-profile role was Lady
Rosamund Painswick on the hit series Downton

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:16.360
Abbey.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:22.699
The Brosnan era also brought with it a new,
female M. Judi Dench played the head of MI6

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.960
as a tough, resourceful woman who could keep
Bond in his place.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:31.160
She was so good that she stayed on into the
Daniel Craig era until M's death in 2012's

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:31.660
Skyfall.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:35.480
And since she is Dame Judi Dench, her career
has kept chugging along.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:39.440
In 2019, she will be seen in adaptations of
Artemis Fowl and Cats.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:47.340
"You get to boss him about and there is a
very special relationship between I think,

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.500
between Bond and M."

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:54.060
Izabella Scorupco was already a successful
model, singer, and actress when she was cast

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.480
as Natalya in 1995's GoldenEye.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:01.600
Her other memorable acting work includes roles
in Exorcist: The Beginning and Reign of Fire.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:06.940
In 2011 she returned to singing with a collaboration
with Swedish vocalist Peter Joback, and in

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.080
2012 she served as host of Sweden's Next Top
Model.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:15.200
Famke Janssen achieved breakout success as
Xenia Onatopp in GoldenEye.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.220
"Xenia Zergevna Onatopp."

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:19.840
"Onatopp?!"

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:20.960
"Onatopp."

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:25.600
The role rocketed her to stardom and helped
land her the role of Jean Grey in the X-Men

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:26.100
franchise.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.960
Since then she's acted regularly in the likes
of Taken and Hemlock Grove.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.680
She will soon be seen in the Netflix original
series Central Park Five.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:39.680
Michelle Yeoh established herself throughout
the 1990s as a major player in Hong Kong action

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:44.060
cinema before breaking out worldwide in 1997's
Tomorrow Never Dies.

00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:49.380
In 2000 she again wowed international audiences
in Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon and has

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:54.200
continued big-screen success ever since, most
recently in Crazy Rich Asians.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.560
Teri Hatcher appeared in Tomorrow Never Dies
as Paris Carver, a former flame of Bond's

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.240
who's now the trophy wife of a villainous
media mogul.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:07.060
She was already a TV superstar with Lois &amp; Clark
and after Bond, she had another big hit in

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:08.640
the form of Desperate Housewives.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:12.469
More recently, she's returned to the world
of DC Comics with a recurring role on The

00:08:12.469 --> 00:08:13.940
CW's Supergirl.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:19.180
Denise Richards was at the height of her fame
when she played Christmas Jones in 1999's

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.280
The World Is Not Enough.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.780
Since then she's continued to appear in plenty
of films and taken on a career as a reality

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:25.820
TV personality.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:30.720
She starred in her own series, Denise Richards:
It's Complicated, and in 2019, she joined

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.580
the cast of The Real Housewives of Beverly
Hills.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:39.640
French actress Sophie Marceau achieved blockbuster
success as the villainous Elektra King in

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:40.560
The World Is Not Enough.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.730
She's continued to work steadily as an actress,
writer, and director ever since.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:49.260
In 2002 she made her feature directorial debut
with Speak To Me of Love.

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:54.020
And in 2015, she served on the main competition
jury for the Cannes Film Festival.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:59.670
Oscar winner Halle Berry was already a major
star when she played Jinx in Pierce Brosnan's

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:02.680
final Bond film, 2002's Die Another Day.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:07.340
Her career has suffered a few missteps along
the way, but she's rebounded and continued

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:09.140
to work steadily in film and TV.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:14.200
Among her most notable projects since Bond
are a return to the X-Men series and Kingsman:

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:15.200
The Golden Circle.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.960
The Daniel Craig era required a memorable
Bond girl to kick things off, and it got one

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.900
with Eva Green as Vesper Lynd in Casino Royale.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:25.100
The role made Green an international star.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:29.720
She's since gone on to roles in the likes
of Penny Dreadful and Miss Peregrine's Home

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:31.070
for Peculiar Children.

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:35.120
In 2019, she can be seen in Tim Burton's live-action
Dumbo remake.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:41.160
After a successful modeling career, Ukrainian-born
French actress Olga Kurylenko landed the role

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:44.480
of Camille Montes in 2008's Quantum of Solace.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:49.480
She has since continued to earn high-profile
roles in films like Oblivion, The Death of

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.460
Stalin, and Johnny English Strikes Again.

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.420
As of 2018, she lives in London with her son
and boyfriend.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:59.160
Naomie Harris was a 10-year veteran of film
acting by the time she landed the part of

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:03.800
the third big-screen Moneypenny in Skyfall,
and she immediately won fans over with her

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:04.300
portrayal.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:08.520
She reprised the role in 2015's Spectre, and
has since garnered acclaim for her work in

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:13.560
Moonlight and appeared in major releases including
Rampage and Mowgli: Legend of the Jungle.

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.420
Léa Seydoux has been acting for more than
a decade, but in many ways her career is still

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:18.920
very young.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:23.930
She achieved international acclaim in 2013
for her role in Blue is the Warmest Color,

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:28.300
and parlayed that into her role as Dr. Madeleine
Swann in 2015's Spectre.

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:33.830
She's expected to reprise her role for the
25th Bond film in 2020, a rare repeat performance

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:34.580
for a Bond girl.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.900
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.960
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:43.480
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

